Z||000023||phillip||06-08-2000||02:51 AM||||chromalusion is the "flip-flop" paint. originaly on mustangs a few years back, but i think they called it mystic. actually i think it usually looks kind of ugly (i think you have to consider if you would want a two tone car that is  the two colors the car is changing, not to mention the colors in between) but the effect is so interesting i like seeing it. i have seen a few nice ones. usually where the effect was more subtle or the color didn't clash so hard. a picture might capture it but you really have to see it in real life to appreciate it.<P>[This message has been edited by phillip (edited 06-08-2000).]<BR><p>[This message has been edited by phillip (edited 06-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000024||stimpy||06-08-2000||06:36 AM||||The chromallusion paint that I would like to get is far less subtle then that purple/babycrap green that Ford sold. You can see it on a lot of custom hotrods nowadays. Ir goes om a vibrant gold to green to purple to red, all depending on the angle of the light. The cool thing about it is there is no pigment in the paint. All the color is caused from refraction of light off of microsopic crystals.  This makes damage repair a whole lot easier.<BR>The downside is is the shtuff is expen$ive. Really expen$ive.||||reg||1
